From 79ab1b66c2e9393d4bce15f9993c5857f4ddef9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:43:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/18] Round 5: Interleave independent reservoir candidates

When no deadline or cancel file is monitored and max_steps covers every
simulated day, the engine passes groups of up to eight untraced
reservoir candidates to a lane kernel that advances them together over
the shared daily inputs, in widths 8, 4 and 1. Scalar and lane paths
share one reservoir_day step, so each candidate performs the same
floating-point operations in the same order and results are
bit-identical; shortage streaks are counted branch-free. Valid
candidates are still charged one logical step per day and invalid ones
none. Workers claim whole groups. New tests compare grouped and guarded
single-candidate runs for full, lean, traced, invalid, partial-group
and multi-worker batches.

Workload: domain2 (48 full reservoir records of 2,400 days), 11
samples against round 4.
Before median: 2.479 ms. After median: 0.802 ms. Speedup: 3.09x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
